# Class Dashboard System

## Core Structure
The class dashboard is implemented in [static/js/class_dashboard.js](mdc:static/js/class_dashboard.js) and provides a comprehensive view of class information with an integrated edit mode.

## Edit Mode Functionality
The dashboard implements a complete edit mode system that allows teachers to modify all aspects of the dashboard:

1. A floating edit button toggles edit mode (`setupEditMode()` function)
2. When active, all editable elements show visual indicators on hover
3. Clicking any editable element shows an inline form for editing that content
4. Changes persist to the Firebase database

## Editable Components
The dashboard supports editing for the following components:

- **Class Header**: Title and description (`createEditHandler()`)
- **Teacher Profile**: Name, email, and profile picture (`editTeacherProfile()`)
- **Syllabus**: Full content editing with rich text (`createEditHandler()`)
- **Office Hours**: Dynamic list with add/remove capability (`editOfficeHours()`)
- **Current Unit**: Title, description, current topic, and progress percentage (`editCurrentUnit()`)
- **Assignments**: Both overview items and detailed cards (`editAssignmentItem()`, `editAssignmentCard()`)
- **Resources**: Complete metadata editing (`editResourceCard()`)
- **Discussion Channels**: Name, privacy settings, and descriptions (`editChannel()`, `editCurrentChannel()`)
- **Student Information**: Name, email, grade level, and profile picture (`editStudentCard()`)

## Firebase Integration
The system integrates with Firebase for persistent storage:

- Each edit function includes database update logic when Firebase is available
- Updates are performed on the appropriate collections based on [database.md](mdc:database.md)
- For complex data like channels and units that exist in arrays within documents, it implements fetch-modify-update patterns

## Tab System
The dashboard uses a tab-based navigation system:
- Overview (default)
- Assignments
- Resources
- Discussions (channels)
- Grades
- Students
- Mind Web visualization

Each tab loads data on demand when first activated through the `loadTabData()` function.

## Database Structure
The Firebase collections used by the class dashboard include:

- **Classes**: Core class information including metadata arrays for channels and units
- **Members**: User accounts including teachers and students
- **Assignments**: Assignment details referenced in the dashboard
- **Resources**: Educational materials shown in the resources tab
- **Messages**: Channel discussion messages
- **Events**: Upcoming class events
